<title>HONG KONG: Hong Kong Countdown Outlook.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong Countdown Outlook.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a countdown of events surrounding the handover of the British colony of Hong Kong to China at midnight on June 30.</p>
<p>=======================================================</p>
<p>MARCH 22</p>
<p>- Provisional legislature meets in Shenzhen.</p>
<p>=======================================================</p>
<p>MARCH 23</p>
<p>- 100 days until Britain hands over Hong Kong to China.</p>
<p>=======================================================</p>
<p>JUNE 3/4</p>
<p>- Hong Kong democracy movement to commemorate 1989 Beijing massacre with overnight candle-light vigil in Victoria Park.</p>
<p>=======================================================</p>
<p>JUNE 30</p>
<p>- Last day of British colonial rule of Hong Kong. Public holiday.</p>
<p>=======================================================</p>
<p>JULY 1</p>
<p>- China resumes sovereignty of Hong Kong. Public holiday.</p>
<p>=======================================================</p>
<p>JULY 2</p>
<p>- Public holiday to mark China's resumption of sovereignty.</p>
<p>=======================================================</p>
<p>DECEMBER 1999</p>
<p>- Administration of Portuguese-run Macau reverts to China.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6352</p>
